              "segment": {
                "start_index": 47,
                "end_index": 248,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "** However, because the parathyroid glands are normally very small (about the size of a grain of rice), they do not usually cause localized neck pain in the way a sore muscle or swollen lymph node does"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2,
                3
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 252,
                "end_index": 429,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Instead, parathyroid issues\u2014most commonly **hyperparathyroidism** (overactive parathyroid glands)\u2014can lead to neck pain through several distinct indirect and direct pathways"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4,
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 444,
                "end_index": 657,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Systemic Bone and Muscle Pain (Most Common)\nHyperparathyroidism causes the body to produce too much parathyroid hormone (PTH), which continuously leaches calcium out of your bones and dumps it into the bloodstream"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4,
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 659,
                "end_index": 855,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "This often leads to:\n* **Cervical Spine Pain:** The loss of calcium can weaken the bones of the spine (osteoporosis or osteopenia), leading to chronic, dull, or deep bone pain in the neck and back"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4,
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 857,
                "end_index": 1064,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Muscle Tension and Spasms:** High calcium levels alter nerve and muscle function, which frequently causes generalized muscle aches, tightness, stiffness, and painful \"knots\" in the neck and shoulder area"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8,
                9
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1074,
                "end_index": 1261,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Local Mass Effects (Less Common)\nWhile most parathyroid adenomas (benign tumors) are tiny, they can sometimes grow large enough to cause physical discomfort in the lower front of the neck"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8,
                10
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1263,
                "end_index": 1331,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "This \"mass effect\" can feel like:\n* A lump or fullness in the throat"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                11,
                10
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1333,
                "end_index": 1396,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* Discomfort when swallowing (dysphagia) or mild local pressure"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                11
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1398,
                "end_index": 1524,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* *Note: In very rare cases, this can be a sign of parathyroid cancer, which presents with a firm neck mass and localized pain"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                12,
                13
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1535,
                "end_index": 1665,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Spontaneous Hemorrhage (Rare, Acute Emergency)\nIn rare instances, a benign parathyroid adenoma can spontaneously rupture and bleed"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                14,
                15
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1667,
                "end_index": 1738,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "This causes a sudden collection of blood (hematoma) in the neck tissues"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                12,
                14,
                15
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1741,
                "end_index": 1900,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Symptoms:** Sudden, severe neck pain, rapid neck swelling, bruising on the neck or upper chest, difficulty swallowing, and potentially difficulty breathing"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                16,
                17
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1974,
                "end_index": 2228,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Post-Surgical Neck Stiffness\nIf you have already been diagnosed with parathyroid disease and recently underwent a **parathyroidectomy** (surgery to remove the overactive gland), localized neck pain, soreness, and stiffness are very common during recovery"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                18
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2230,
                "end_index": 2349,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "This is usually due to the positioning of your neck during the operation and surgical manipulation of the local muscles"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                19
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2357,
                "end_index": 2570,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "### Connecting the Dots: Other Symptoms to Watch For\nBecause chronic neck pain is so common and often caused by simple muscle strain, doctors look for other symptoms of hyperparathyroidism to help make a diagnosis"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2572,
                "end_index": 2695,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "These are often remembered by the medical adage **\"stones, bones, groans, and psychic moans\"**:\n* **Stones:** Kidney stones"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                8
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2697,
                "end_index": 2748,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Bones:** Joint and bone pain, or easy fractures"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2750,
                "end_index": 2813,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Groans:** Nausea, vomiting, constipation, or abdominal pain"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                4,
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2815,
                "end_index": 2902,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Psychic Moans:** Severe fatigue, brain fog, depression, or difficulty concentrating"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            }
